{
  "origin": "Robert Izquierdo, The Motley Fool, article published August 1, 2026 at 9:05 p.m. EST. The article attributes its revenue series to company filings and says the data are as of July 31, 2026; it does not give a separate statement date for the quoted next-quarter forecast.",
  "note": "The article reports NVIDIA revenue of $81.6 billion for the period ended July 2026, up from $30.0 billion for the period ended July 2024, and says NVIDIA forecast revenue of $91 billion for the next quarter. It also says NVIDIA’s Vera Rubin platform is expected to contribute to ongoing sales growth and identifies Alphabet as one of NVIDIA’s customers. These reported results and the company forecast, as relayed by a third-party article, support a view of strong recent sales and expected near-term growth, consistent with demand for NVIDIA’s offerings. Alphabet’s customer status is relevant demand context, but the article gives no NVIDIA revenue or orders attributable to Alphabet. The forecast is not a realized result, and the article does not provide its assumptions.",
  "limitations": [
    "The article provides no NVIDIA revenue breakdown that quantifies AI-related sales or separates Vera Rubin’s expected contribution.",
    "It does not state the assumptions behind the $91 billion forecast or provide customer-level sales or order data."
  ],
  "follow_up": [
    "Check NVIDIA’s filing and earnings guidance for the period ended July 2026 to verify the $81.6 billion result and the $91 billion next-quarter forecast, then compare the forecast with the reported result.",
    "Review NVIDIA’s subsequent filings and product updates for reported AI/data-center revenue and Vera Rubin shipment or revenue milestones."
  ],
  "proposal": null
}
